WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.636
&gt;&gt;&gt; THE FAA
LAUNCHING AN INVESTIGATION AFTER

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:07.006
TWO PLANES NEARLY COLLIDED ON
THE RUNWAY.

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:17.817
ONE PLANE ABOUT TO TAKEOFF,
ANOTHER CROSSING IN FRONT OF IT.

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:21.721
PETE MUNTEAN JOINS ME NOW.
THINK ABOUT IT ALL THE TIME,

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:24.724
ESPECIALLY AT BUSY AIRPORTS.
HOW DID IT GET THIS CLOSE?

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:28.394
&gt;&gt; Reporter: SECONDS TO SPARE
BUT THE GOOD NEWS IS THIS WAS

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:31.731
AVOIDED THANKS TO THE QUICK
THINKING OF THE AIR TRAFFIC

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:35.602
CONTROLLER IN THE TOWER AT JFK
AND THE QUICK REACTION BY THE

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:39.672
DELTA CREW ON BOARD THE 737.
THIS IS THE ANIMATION FROM

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.008
FLIGHT RADAR 24.
YOU CAN SEE THE DELTA FLIGHT

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:48.181
THERE WAS ABOUT TO TAKEOFF ON
RUNWAY 4 LEFT THERE AT JFK WHEN

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:52.152
AN AMERICAN AIRLINES FLIGHT
CROSSED IN FRONT OF IT.

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:55.855
LISTEN TO THE URGENCY BY THE AIR
TRAFFIC CONTROLLER IN THE TOWER

00:00:55.855 --> 00:01:00.093
WARNING THE CREW OF THAT DELTA
FLIGHT TO SLAM ON THE BRAKES AND

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:04.430
STOP TO MAKE SURE THEY DON'T HIT
THAT OTHER PLANE TAXIING ACROSS

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:11.838
THE RUNWAY.
&gt;&gt; DELTA, 1943, CANCEL TAKEOFF

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:14.807
PLANS.
DELTA 1943 CANCEL TAKEOFF PLANS.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:19.412
&gt;&gt; REJECTING.
&gt;&gt; Reporter: THE FAA SAYS ABOUT

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:22.849
1,000 FEET OF SEPARATION BETWEEN
THE TWO PLANES IN THE END.

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:28.188
SOUNDS LIKE A LOT BUT IT'S ABOUT
THREE FOOTBALL FIELDS BUT PRETTY

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:32.559
CLOSE IN AVIATION TERMS.
THIS IS A RUN WAY INCURSION.

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:37.630
THESE HAPPEN ALL THE TIME
ACCORDING TO THE FAA, 1600 OF

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.532
THEM IN 2022, TYPICALLY NOT AS
DRAMATIC AS THIS ONE, ALTHOUGH

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:44.971
THE CONSEQUENCES ARE WRITTEN IN
BLOOD, THE DISASTER IN 1977, TWO

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:48.174
747s HIT EACH OTHER ON THE
RUNWAY.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:52.278
500 PEOPLE KILLED, THE SINGLE
WORST AIRPLANE CLASH IN AVIATION

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:57.817
HISTORY, POPPY.
&gt;&gt; THAT DELTA PILOT, CALM.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:01.788
&gt;&gt; VERY CALM.
CAN I ASK YOU SOMETHING PETE.

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:04.991
THE DELTA PLANE WAS ABOUT TO
TAKE OFF.

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:08.361
WAS IT GAINING MOMENTUM OR WAS
IT THE BEGINNING OF THE TAXI?

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:10.563
&gt;&gt; Reporter: THEY WERE
ACCELERATING FOR TAKEOFF.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:14.000
THIS IS SOMETHING THAT PILOTS
PRACTICE ALL THE TIME IN THE

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.103
SIMULATOR.
THEY'RE TYPICALLY NOT OFTEN

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:19.505
CONFRONTED WITH IT IN REAL LIFE.
SO THEY WERE JUST ABOUT BEFORE

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:24.010
THE SPEED THAT YOU NEED TO
TAKEOFF, YOU HAVE TO COMMIT AT A

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:27.146
CERTAIN POINT SO ONCE YOU HIT
THE SPEED YOU HAVE TO KEEP

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:30.349
FLYING.
THEY DID NOT GET THERE JUST YET

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:32.952
SO THEY WERE ABLE TO STOP AND
DECELERATE.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:35.054
STOP BEFORE THE 777 STILL ON THE
RUNWAY.

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:40.226
LET'S DISCUSS WITH FORMER
DEPARTMENT OF TRANSPORTATION

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:44.831
INSPECTOR, MARY SCIAVO.
WHAT IS YOUR REACTION TO THIS?

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:48.468
&gt;&gt; IT'S NOT MY REACTION.
WHAT HAPPENED HERE FALLS INTO

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:54.374
THE MOST SERIOUS CATEGORY OF
RUNWAY INCURSIONS, AND THEY

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:59.245
DIVIDE THEM UP THROUGH THE
SERIOUSNESS OF A, B, C AND D,

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:01.414
AND THIS IS THE TOP, THIS IS THE
MOST SERIOUS.

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:06.419
THERE ARE ABOUT 20 OF THESE MOST
SERIOUS CATEGORIES, A AND B

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:16.229
EVERY YEAR, AND THE MORE
DISTURBING STATISTIC, RUNWAY

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.331
IN
IN

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:21.868
INCURSIONS HAVE BEEN UP 92% FROM
2011 UNTIL 2018.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:26.372
SO THIS IS A HUGE ISSUE WITH THE
GOVERNMENT, WITH THE FAA AND MY

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:31.644
OLD OFFICE, THE OFFICE OF
INSPECTOR GENERAL.

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:36.482
THIS IS ONE STATISTIC ON THE
RISE AND IT'S NOT A STATISTIC

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:37.583
YOU WANT TO SEE RISE.
IT'S A PROBLEM.

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:41.521
&gt;&gt; WHY IS IT ON THE RISE?
&gt;&gt; WELL, MANY REASONS.

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:46.225
I MEAN, OBVIOUSLY AVIATION HAS
INCREASED OVER THE YEARS, BUT

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:49.429
THE STUDIES HAVE LOOKED INTO WHY
THIS IS OCCURRING BLAME MANY

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:52.498
DIFFERENT THINGS.
THERE HAVE BEEN MANY KINDS OF

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:56.202
DIFFERENT EQUIPMENT AND MANY
PROGRAMS THE FAA PROPOSED.

00:03:56.202 --> 00:04:02.075
THEY PUT SOME FORTH, AND ONE WAS
CALLED A-MASS, AND IT WAS

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:05.945
NICKNAMED AMASS, AND IT WAS
SCRAPPED AND NOW THEY USE

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:09.415
DETECTION EQUIPMENT AND THEY ARE
WORKING ON SPECIALIZED RUNWAY

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:13.353
LIGHTING TO GIVE PILOTS AND AIR
TRAFFIC CONTROLLERS CLUES AS TO

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:18.424
WHEN THERE'S AN INTERSECTION.
A LOT OF THESE PROGRAMS HAVE

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:21.227
BEEN ON DEVELOPMENT A LONG TIME.
NOT ALL OF THE AIRCRAFT ARE

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:25.898
EQUIPPED WITH THEM.
AIRCRAFT CARRIERS ARE EQUIPPED

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:31.838
WITH THE MOST MODERN EQUIPMENT,
AND MOST RUNWAY INCURSIONS,

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:38.044
ABOUT 60%, OCCUR AT TOWERED
AIRPORTS, AIRPORTS WITH A TOWER.

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:42.515
YOU WOULD THINK THEY WOULD
HAPPEN AT NON-TOWERED AIRPORTS.

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:49.422
THIS IS A PROBLEM THAT HAS BEEN
ON THE RADAR SCREEN, AND IT'S A

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:51.591
STATISTIC THEY ARE WORRIED ABOUT
TRYING TO BRING DOWN.

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:54.227
THIS WAS THE MOST SERIOUS
CATEGORY OF ALL.

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:57.730
&gt;&gt; REALLY ALARMING.
MARY, THANK YOU.

